{
  "dom_id": "step-q156096",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+4>6 \\\\ 4-x\\ge 2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $k$ that satisfy both $2x+4>6$ and $4-x\\ge 2$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $2x+4>6:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+4 & >6 \\\\ 2x+4-4 & >6-4 \\\\ 2x & >2 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & >\\frac{2}{2} \\\\ x & >1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14224662/assets/6d3b61147527a632ccb46629a356e9f5c92a1ddfc8a52f3d0890cd46eb56f564.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $4-x\\ge 2:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-x & \\ge 2 \\\\ 4-x-4 & \\ge 2-4 \\\\ -x & \\ge -2 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-x) & \\le (-1)\\cdot (-2) \\\\ x & \\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14224662/assets/1452391c950b051c4cf454723498e6fa657f6d5f1315f78e50f3450bf7fbc1eb.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14224662/assets/a22a207cc64d33470e27d0b1f45ad0b87106fafd67b88c2163524a44951639bf.png)\n\n    \n\nThus, the final solution is $x\\in (1,2].$",
